### Rotating Card (CSS + HTML)

Below is a minimal example of a card that rotates 180 degrees around its Y‑axis when you hover over it.  
Feel free to adjust the size, colors, or animation duration to fit your design.

```html
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<meta charset="UTF-8">
<title>Hover‑Rotate Card</title>
<style>
/* ---------- Container (optional) ---------- */
.card-wrapper {
  perspective: 1000px;          /* gives depth to the 3D effect */
  width: 300px;
  margin: 50px auto;
}

/* ---------- Card ---------- */
.card {
  width: 100%;
  height: 200px;
  background: #fff;
  border-radius: 12px;
  box-shadow: 0 10px 20px rgba(0,0,0,.2);
  transition: transform 0.6s ease;   /* smooth rotation */
  transform-style: preserve-3d;      /* keep children in 3D space */
  cursor: pointer;
}

/* ---------- Hover effect ---------- */
.card:hover {
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* rotate 180° around Y axis */
}

/* ---------- Front & Back faces ---------- */
.card::before,
.card::after {
  content: "";
  position: absolute;
  inset: 0;
  backface-visibility: hidden;      /* hide back face when rotated */
  border-radius: 12px;
}

.card::before {                      /* front face */
  background: #4CAF50;
  color: #fff;
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: bold;
}

.card::after {                       /* back face */
  background: #2196F3;
  color: #fff;
  transform: rotateY(180deg);        /* flip back face so it shows correctly */
  display: flex;
  align-items: center;
  justify-content: center;
  font-size: 1.5rem;
  font-weight: bold;
}
</style>
</head>
<body>

<div class="card-wrapper">
  <div class="card"></div>
</div>

</body>
</html>
```

#### How it works

| Element | Purpose |
|---------|---------|
| `.card-wrapper` | Sets a `perspective` so the 3D rotation looks realistic. |
| `.card` | The main element that will rotate. `transform-style: preserve-3d` keeps child elements in 3D space. |
| `::before` / `::after` | Two pseudo‑elements representing the front and back faces of the card. |
| `backface-visibility: hidden` | Hides the backside of each face when it’s turned away from the viewer. |
| `transform: rotateY(180deg)` on hover | Rotates the card 180 degrees around the Y‑axis. |

You can replace the pseudo‑elements with real `<div>` children if you need more complex content on each side. Just remember to set `backface-visibility: hidden` on those children as well. Enjoy!
